cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the preferred citation below."
title: beNNch
abstract: >-
  beNNch is a modular framework for performance benchmarking of neuronal network
  simulations. Version 1.x provides a workflow for reproducible, comparable
  benchmarks of simulation engines such as NEST. Version 2.0 ("CI-beNNch")
  restructures the framework around continuous benchmarking: it takes a
  declarative benchmark configuration from a researcher, generates a GitLab CI
  pipeline from it, and executes the resulting benchmark jobs autonomously on
  HPC systems.
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: "2.0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-12"
repository-code: "https://github.com/INM-6/beNNch"
url: "https://inm-6.github.io/beNNch"
keywords:
  - benchmarking
  - continuous benchmarking
  - continuous integration
  - high-performance computing
  - neuronal network simulation
  - computational neuroscience
  - NEST simulator
  - reproducibility
  - performance engineering
  - research software engineering

